IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`

-- je21-art15-16-revision-publication: Articles 15(8), 15(9) and 16 of the Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021 (L.8/2021).
-- 15(1) to (7) and (10) are in the coverage table of NOTES.md: the Board's constitution and procedure are `out-of-scope` or `inert`, and 15(4) to (7) are in je21-schedule1.l4.
-- 16 Publication of legislation.
--
-- 15(9) says the Board's minutes "must be laid before the States within 2 months of the business being transacted".
-- A period in calendar months is counted by the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954's definition of "month", which this encoding does not use and may not apply,
-- so the model does not add months to a date: the caller gives the last day on which the minutes could be laid, worked out under that Law, and the model compares.
--
-- 16(1)(a) turns on "after the commencement of this Part", which for legislation made on 28 September 2021 itself depends on the time at which Part 3 came into force: fork L3.
-- 16(1)(b) turns on "after 1st January 2019", taken as the days after that day.

§ `Article 15 -- Changes that may be made by the Law Revision Board in revising Jersey legislation`

-- Answers: do the changes made to legislation by a revision have effect as if they were effected by an amendment made by other legislation?
-- They do, for a revision: legislation certified as revised legislation under Article 15(7).
-- A draft that has not been certified is not a revision, and the Law does not say what its changes do.
-- src:158 | (8) The changes made to legislation by a revision have effect as if they were effected by an amendment made by other legislation.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 15(8) (src:158)
GIVEN `the draft revision has been certified as revised legislation under Article 15(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 15(8): the changes made by the revision have effect as if effected by an amendment made by other legislation` `the draft revision has been certified as revised legislation under Article 15(7)` MEANS
    IF `the draft revision has been certified as revised legislation under Article 15(7)`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE REFUSE "Article 15(8) speaks of the changes made by a revision, and the Law does not say what the changes in a draft that has not been certified do"

-- Answers: were the minutes laid before the States within the time Article 15(9) allows?
-- The caller gives the day they were laid and the last day on which they could be laid "within 2 months of the business being transacted", counted under the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954.
-- Laid on the last day is within.
-- src:159 | (9) The Minutes or other record of the transactions of the business of the Law Revision Board must be laid before the States within 2 months of the business being transacted.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 15(9) (src:159)
GIVEN `the day on which the minutes were laid before the States` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which they could be laid within 2 months of the business being transacted` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 15(9): the minutes were laid in time` `the day on which the minutes were laid before the States` `the last day on which they could be laid within 2 months of the business being transacted` MEANS
    `the day on which the minutes were laid before the States` AT MOST `the last day on which they could be laid within 2 months of the business being transacted`

§ `Article 16 -- Publication of legislation`

§§ `16(1) What must be published`

-- Answers: must the Principal Legislative Drafter ensure that this legislation is published?
-- (a) All as-enacted legislation made after the commencement of Part 3.
-- (b) All consolidated legislation (revised legislation is consolidated legislation, 12(4)) prepared after 1 January 2019.
-- The caller gives the day it was made (as-enacted) or prepared (consolidated or revised).
-- For (a), the edge day 28 September 2021 depends on fork L3.
-- For (b), the edge day 1 January 2019 is not after itself.
-- src:162 | (1) The Principal Legislative Drafter must ensure that the following are published –
-- src:163 | (a) all as-enacted legislation made after the commencement of this Part;
-- src:164 | (b) all consolidated legislation prepared after 1st January 2019.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 16(1) (src:162-164)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of text under Part 3`
      `the day on which it was made or prepared` IS A DATE
      reading IS A `Reading L3 of the time at which the Law came into force`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Article 16(1): the Principal Legislative Drafter must ensure that the legislation is published` kind `the day on which it was made or prepared` reading MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `as-enacted legislation`
        THEN
            BRANCH
                IF `the day on which it was made or prepared` LESS THAN YMD 2021 9 28 THEN FALSE
                IF `the day on which it was made or prepared` GREATER THAN YMD 2021 9 28 THEN TRUE
                OTHERWISE
                    CONSIDER reading
                    WHEN `the beginning of 28 September 2021, by Article 3(2)` THEN TRUE
                    WHEN `the sources do not state it, so a question that turns on a time of day on 28 September 2021 is refused`
                        THEN REFUSE "the sources do not say at what time of day on 28 September 2021 Part 3 of the Law came into force, so whether legislation made that day was made after it cannot be answered"
    WHEN `consolidated legislation` THEN `the day on which it was made or prepared` GREATER THAN YMD 2019 1 1
    WHEN `revised legislation` THEN `the day on which it was made or prepared` GREATER THAN YMD 2019 1 1

§§ `16(2) When it must be published`

-- Answers: from what day does "as soon as practicable" run for publication?
-- As-enacted legislation "as soon as practicable after it is made": from the day it was made.
-- Consolidated legislation "as soon as practicable after it is consolidated or the amendments resulting from other legislation are incorporated within it, whichever is the later": from the later of those two days.
-- What counts as "as soon as practicable" is a judgement; the model gives the day it runs from and no deadline.
-- src:165 | (2) As-enacted legislation must be published as soon as practicable after it is made and consolidated legislation must be published as soon as practicable after it is consolidated or the amendments resulting from other legislation are incorporated within it, whichever is the later.
@ref Legislation (Jersey) Law 2021, Article 16(2) (src:165)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of text under Part 3`
      `the day on which the legislation was made, or consolidated` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the amendments resulting from other legislation were incorporated` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`Article 16(2): the day from which publication is due as soon as practicable` kind `the day on which the legislation was made, or consolidated` `the day on which the amendments resulting from other legislation were incorporated` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `as-enacted legislation` THEN `the day on which the legislation was made, or consolidated`
    WHEN `consolidated legislation`
        THEN IF `the day on which the legislation was made, or consolidated` AT LEAST `the day on which the amendments resulting from other legislation were incorporated`
             THEN `the day on which the legislation was made, or consolidated`
             ELSE `the day on which the amendments resulting from other legislation were incorporated`
    WHEN `revised legislation`
        THEN IF `the day on which the legislation was made, or consolidated` AT LEAST `the day on which the amendments resulting from other legislation were incorporated`
             THEN `the day on which the legislation was made, or consolidated`
             ELSE `the day on which the amendments resulting from other legislation were incorporated`
